{"seconds": 29.4, "exit": 0, "final": "The key point is clear: **Rf5+** forces the king to move, and if **Kg6**, then **Qh5# is mate**. This is the knockout punch.\n\n**Best move:** Rf5+\n\n**Main line:** 1. Rf5+ Kg6 (forced, as Ke7 and Ke6 are also losing but slower) 2. Qh5#\n\n**Motif:** fork (or more precisely, this is a forcing check that drives the king into a mating net)\n\n**Coaching note (80 words max):**\n\nWhen your opponent's king is exposed on an open file or diagonal, look for forcing checks that drive it into worse positions. Here, **Rf5+ checks the king on f6**, forcing it to move. If **Kg6**, then **Qh5 is checkmate** because the rook on f5 controls escape squares and the queen delivers mate with the king's own pawns blocking retreat. Always calculate checks on exposed kings before other moves\u2014they often force the opponent into tactical disasters.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rf5+\", \"line\": [\"Rf5+\", \"Kg6\", \"Qh5#\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28", "move": "Rd6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28", "move": "Rf5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q3k2/3R4/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 w - - 5 28", "move": "Qe6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q1R1k2/8/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 b - - 6 28", "move": "Qxd6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5nr/p1p3pp/1q1R1k2/8/8/2bB3Q/P3KP1P/8 b - - 6 28", "move": "cxd6"}}, {"tool"